        "text": "Base rate/reference class: recent G.17 monthly total-index percent changes are centered near modest growth. The seven-observation volatility sample uses latest available current/revised G.17 values, not first-vintage-only history; that is a limitation for a strict first-print target but should still capture typical one-month total-index dispersion. The last seven values Nov 2025-May 2026 are -0.2, 0.5, -0.4, 0.8, -0.3, 0.9, and 0.1, giving a simple recent reference class mean about 0.2 percent, while the latest May reading of 0.1 percent and flat manufacturing argue against extrapolating April's 0.9 percent jump."
